        "CopyrightInformation": "© The Author(s) 2015.",
        "AbstractText": "Intrathoracic goiter is not uncommon but one that requires a sternotomy in addition to a cervical incision, to aid its removal, is. We describe the case of a 51-year-old woman whose intrathoracic goiter was successfully removed via a sternotomy."
